.DS_Store
.envrc
.env*
!.env.enc
!.env.example

# Raw fetch payloads are reproducible via scripts/ and pruned after 28 days —
# never committed. Both trees are covered so the data/sources -> data/raw rename
# cannot leak payloads, and ALL extensions are covered (the old .json-only rule
# was committing .rss/.xml/.jsonl payloads — ~19MB/day once ingest runs hourly).
# The per-run manifest stays: it is the human-readable record of what each fetch did.
# Level 1 catches stray files written straight into the tree (runner logs);
# the !*/ rules keep the dated directories traversable so the manifest survives.
data/sources/*
data/raw/*
!data/sources/*/
!data/raw/*/
data/sources/*/*
data/raw/*/*
!data/sources/*/manifest.md
!data/raw/*/manifest.md

# data/lookup/ IS NOT LISTED HERE, AND THAT IS THE POINT. It looks like fetch
# output and it is not: it is the enrichment corpus (CONVENTIONS.md "Lookup
# layer"), ~600 HTTP requests to rebuild, and its whole job is to still exist
# next quarter when a gap-check asks what the CZ e-commerce add-on market held.
# Putting it under data/raw/ would have gitignored it AND pruned it at 28 days.
# Do not widen the rules above to `data/*` — that would swallow it silently.

# The working store: deterministically rebuildable from the committed ledgers.
data/register.db
data/register.db-wal
data/register.db-shm

# Bytecode. scripts/model_pass.py imports normalize.py so the two halves of the
# model seam cannot drift on SECTORS or is_material(), and that import is what
# creates scripts/__pycache__/. It is a build artefact of running the pipeline,
# never a record of it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vercel
